# __LIBRARY_NAME__

__DESCRIPTION__

## Compatibility

- Arduino framework
- PlatformIO platform: `__PLATFORM__`
- Arduino architecture: `__ARCHITECTURES__`

## Installation with PlatformIO

After publication to the PlatformIO Registry, add the package to your project:

```ini
lib_deps =
    controlandoeletrons/__LIBRARY_NAME__ @ __VERSION__
```

## Basic usage

```cpp
#include <__LIBRARY_NAME__.h>

__LIBRARY_NAME__ library;

void setup() {
    library.begin();
}

void loop() {}
```

See `package/examples/BasicUsage` for the complete example.

## Development

Open `development/` as the PlatformIO project. Edit the library implementation
only in `package/src/`; the project consumes it through
`symlink://../package`.

Build locally with:

```powershell
cd __LIBRARY_NAME__\development
pio run
```

## Versioning

This library follows Semantic Versioning. Use tags in the form
`__LIBRARY_NAME__-vX.Y.Z`, keeping the tag version equal to the version in both
files under `package/`.
